            <ArticleTitle>[Bronchogenic cyst of the right hemidiaphragm mimicking a hydatic cyst of the liver].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1224-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Ectopic subdiaphragmatic development of a bronchogenic cyst is rare. We report the case of a 28-year-old woman with a symptomatic bronchogenic cyst of the right hemidiaphragm simulating a hydatic cyst of the liver on ultrasonography and CT scan. Diagnosis of a diaphragmatic lesion was made during laparotomy, and complete resection was successful. Final diagnosis was done on pathology.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
